<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Bursa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1326">1326</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-ottoman-wars">Byzantine–Ottoman wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bursa">Bursa</a> was the long Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naval-blockade">blockade</a> of the Byzantine city of Bursa in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, which surrendered in 1326 to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orhan">Orhan</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osman-i">Osman I</a>. Bursa became the first major Ottoman capital. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> treat its capture as a key step in the foundation of the Ottoman state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siege-of-bursa.jpg" alt="Siege of Bursa" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Citrat at Turkish Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bursa_Kalesi_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
